  },
  {
    src: '/images/vinyl-sdt-tile-lab-columns-view.jpg',
    alt: 'White resilient SDT tile floor with columns and wall panels',
    caption: 'Columns and wall panels',
  },
  {
    src: '/images/vinyl-sdt-tile-lab-clean-white-floor.jpg',
    alt: 'Clean white resilient SDT tile floor',
    caption: 'Clean finished tile floor',
  },
  {
    src: '/images/vinyl-sdt-tile-lab-doorway-view.jpg',
    alt: 'Resilient SDT tile floor toward a doorway',
    caption: 'Toward the doorway',
  },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'What types of flooring do you install?',
    answer:
      'We install hardwood, engineered wood, ceramic tile, porcelain tile, natural stone, carpet, carpet tile, and luxury vinyl tile and plank (LVT/LVP). We source products from leading manufacturers including Mohawk, Shaw, Arizona Tile, and Daltile. Contact us at (623) 688-8422 for a free estimate on any flooring type.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you offer free estimates?',
    answer:
      'Yes, we offer free in-home estimates with no obligation. We visit your home or business anywhere in the Phoenix metro area, measure your space, discuss your options, and provide a detailed written estimate. Call (623) 688-8422 or use our online contact form to schedule.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does a typical flooring installation take?',
    answer:
      'A single room of carpet or luxury vinyl can often be completed in one day. Tile and hardwood projects for an average-sized home typically take 2 to 5 days. Larger residential remodels and commercial projects in Chandler, Tempe, Mesa, or other Valley locations may take a week or more. We provide a detailed timeline during your free estimate.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you offer warranties on your installations?',
    answer:
      'Yes, we stand behind every installation with a workmanship warranty. In addition, most products we install carry manufacturer warranties from brands like Mohawk, Shaw, Arizona Tile, and Daltile. We explain all warranty coverage during your free estimate so there are no surprises.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What are the best pet-friendly flooring options?',
    answer:
      'Luxury vinyl plank (LVP) and porcelain tile are the most popular pet-friendly choices. LVP is waterproof, scratch-resistant, and easy to clean. Porcelain tile is extremely durable and resists scratches and stains. We help homeowners across Scottsdale, Mesa, Peoria, and the entire Phoenix area choose flooring that works for families with pets.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you work on commercial flooring projects?',
    answer:
      'Yes, we provide professional flooring services for commercial clients throughout the Valley. We have completed projects for property management companies, general contractors, retail stores, offices, and restaurants in Phoenix, Glendale, Scottsdale, Chandler, and surrounding cities. Contact us for a free commercial estimate.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What areas do you serve?',
    answer:
      'We serve the entire Greater Phoenix Area including Phoenix, Glendale, Scottsdale, Mesa, Chandler, Tempe, Peoria, Surprise, Avondale, Goodyear, and surrounding communities. Our home base is in Glendale, and we typically service locations within a 50-mile radius.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How should I prepare for installation day?',
    answer:
      'Clear furniture and personal items from the rooms being worked on. Remove wall decorations and fragile items near the work area. Ensure the space is accessible and keep pets and children away from the installation zone. Our team handles the rest, including removing old flooring if that is part of your project. We provide detailed preparation instructions during your free estimate appointment.',
  },
];

const allServices = [
